<title>GERMANY: Vereinte 1996 pretax profit up 22 percent.</title>
<headline>Vereinte 1996 pretax profit up 22 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit on ord. activities    228     vs 187</p>
<p>    Premium income (gross)		   8,122   vs 7,910</p>
<p>    Gross claims paid			  5,144   vs 5,272</p>
<p>    Earnings from investments		2,125   vs 2,102</p>
<p>    Underwriting profit			91	vs 71</p>
<p>    DVFA earnings per share		  36.25   vs 28.95 dmk</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurer is Vereinte Versicherungsgruppe, fully owned by Allianz AG, Germany's biggest insurance group. Vereinte also said it had acquired some 100,000 new clients in its health insurance business through its association with Allianz.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
